{:schema :wm/eig-outcome-class-mapping-v1
 :disposition
 OUTCOME-CLASS-MAPPING-DECLARED
 :for-split "resources/wm/eig/held-out-split-v2.edn"
 :ticket/id "T-repair-occ-444fb018cbbb656d09b8f4f67c063f1d51a1932a9b1c281d999c567cf22a2ade"
 :registered-at "2026-09-23T18:05:00Z"
 :declared-by "claude-5"

 ;; WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. held-out-split-v2 declares four outcome classes
 ;; -- :result :no-result :failure :timeout -- and the runner records a
 ;; different vocabulary (:grounded-change, :grounded-no-change,
 ;; :artifact-only, and the failure/timeout endings). Nothing declared how
 ;; one maps onto the other, so a collector would have had to invent the
 ;; mapping at the moment it read the outcomes. That is the step where a
 ;; preregistration stops being one.
 :reason "v2 declared the outcome alphabet but not how the runner's recorded outcomes map onto it."

 ;; DISCLOSURE, stated because it is the thing a reader should be able to
 ;; check. This mapping is registered when ONE of the window's two
 ;; observations already exists: run 2026-09-23-1790184736 closed
 ;; :grounded-no-change. It is registered before the second, and before any
 ;; calibration is computed -- the bounds in v2 gate the calibration limb,
 ;; and that is what this is prospective with respect to.
 :observations-already-recorded ["2026-09-23-1790184736"]
 :prospective-with-respect-to :calibration-evaluation

 ;; The mapping is the literal reading of v2's four class names: an
 ;; attempt that grounded a change produced a result; one that ran to a
 ;; durable close and grounded no change produced no result; one that
 ;; failed or refused is a failure; one that ran out of time is a timeout.
 ;; It is stated exhaustively so no recorded outcome can be silently
 ;; unclassified, and so it cannot be re-read after the fact.
 :mapping {:grounded-change :result
           :grounded-no-change :no-result
           :artifact-only :no-result
           :refused :failure
           :service-failed :failure
           :error :failure
           :timeout :timeout}

 ;; An outcome outside the map is NOT coerced to a class. It is retained
 ;; with this status and does not count toward the window, which keeps an
 ;; unforeseen ending visible instead of absorbing it into :no-result.
 :unmapped-outcome :unclassified-outcome-not-counted

 :claims {:observations-collected? false
          :calibration-evidence-present? false
          :restoration-accepted? false}}
